  "request": "Generate a 12-frame player dancing spritesheet on a 128x128 calibration tile at exactly 12 fps. Keep one player design with nominal 160px standing height, the same anatomy scale and floor-center foot/root anchor in every frame. Remove the calibration floor, retain complete limbs, and deliver a playable loop. Deliver each sprite in a 192x320px frame with local projected ground anchor (96,248). Arrange the isolated source panels in 4 columns and 3 rows, in the stated frame order. Save original generated images, exact prompts, all references, processed sprites, result.json, and review previews in /Users/yiouchen/.codex/worktrees/1834/tile-foundry/assets/evals/2026-10-16-chroma-processing/dancing-player.",
  "criteria": {
    "projection": "Screen-aligned square grid; top and front readable; parallel edges, no depth-dependent scale or camera drift.",
    "complete-art": "Full silhouette and effects fit the declared frame; no clipped limbs or undeclared shadows.",
    "anchor-placement": "Ground/root location matches the guide independently of alpha bounds or visible toe tips.",
    "same-player": "Face, outfit, palette, limb lengths, camera and lighting stay consistent.",
    "dancing-poses": "Twelve distinct useful dance poses form a readable loop without fused/missing limbs.",
    "design-height": "Nominal anatomy/standing height stays constant; crouches and raised arms legitimately change the silhouette bounds and must not be resized to a common bounding box.",
    "contact-stability": "Projected ground root stays at the floor center; no per-frame anchor fitting or image rescaling.",
    "cutout-quality": "Inspect light/dark backgrounds for floor residue, color spill, holes and clipped shoes.",
    "loop": "Last-to-first transition has no unintended pop or scale jump.",
    "source-faithfulness": "Compare original generated sources with processed sprites and declared operations; no invented replacement art or unreported geometry fitting."
